 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "the same propagator carries the same index on both ends"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c1836544-701c-413c-a270-bf06f82b886b"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"One caution\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"18959e19-b84f-47a9-9822-13ea14170dea"],
 "\nThis line: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Spinor", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\"Spin\"", ",", "_", ",", "mp_"}], "]"}], " ", "/;", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mp", "===", 
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"diag", "[", "\"InternalEdgeIndices\"", "]"}], "[", 
              "edge", "]"}], "[", "vertex", "]"}]}]}]], "ChatCode", "Input", 
     LanguageCategory -> "Input", ShowAutoStyles -> True, 
     ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> True, 
     TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "19f2ba7c-ee81-4d2e-9988-ab17f1b6a190"],
 "\nassumes the relevant internal spinor argument is exactly the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["Multiparticle[...]", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "5820e229-a2c5-465c-8580-d12eb7dce544"],
 " stored in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["diag[\"InternalEdgeIndices\"]", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "f88b9e61-ee88-4253-9dfb-5751b42cfa5b"],
 ". From your earlier code, that appears to be correct. If HEPCAT sometimes \
wraps that object differently, we may need to broaden the match. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"If you want\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"210daca1-2ed1-4641-92fa-f1133759e522"],
 "\nI can give you a cleaner, shorter version next that: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "computes the edge-index multiplicities more robustly,"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"d36ca666-1d05-4929-8c9f-3f9d97e4a387"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "stores spin-index data directly in the propagator record,"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"fd5e669c-9d9c-439c-87ca-830f6f13955b"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "and integrates this automatically into ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
    "CreateDiagrams", "paclet:ref/CreateDiagrams", 
     "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/CreateDiagrams.html"},
    "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"45680fab-1b40-48c1-aac2-c558b67c8fa6"],
  "-style output so ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell["diagramAmplitude[diag]", Background -> None]},
    "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
   "5a9f2f2f-36f8-49f8-8841-0920745a3c2a"],
  " needs no second argument."
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"1f04cbb1-3435-4c86-8228-b28235572702"]
}], "ChatOutput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "Yes \[LongDash] the issue is that the current code assigns indices \
independently inside each vertex, so the two ends of the same internal \
propagator do **not** share the same spin index, and the upper/lower \
assignment is being inferred too loosely.\n\nWhat you want instead is:\n\n1. \
assign one unique index per internal propagator, not per spinor occurrence\n\
2. use that same index on both ends of that propagator\n3. determine variance \
from the endpoint label on that propagator:\n   * particle end $$\\to$$ \
``\"Upper\"``\n   * antiparticle end $$\\to$$ ``\"Lower\"``\n4. if a given \
endpoint contributes two spinors with the same ``Multiparticle[...]`` then \
use two indices for that propagator and symmetrize\n\nSo the logic has to be \
based on the actual internal edge, not just the local vertex expression.\n\n\
Here is a corrected version.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\n\t  \
spinIndexSymbolsForEdge,\n\t  spinorVarianceAtEndpoint,\n\t  \
symmetrizeIndices,\n\t  makeVertexSpinIndicesExplicit,\n\t  \
makeDiagramSpinIndicesExplicit\n\t]\n\t\nspinIndexSymbolsForEdge[edge_, \
multiplicity_Integer] := \n\t  Array[Symbol[\"i\" <> ToString[#]] &, \
multiplicity]\n\t\nspinorVarianceAtEndpoint[\n\t  vertex_,\n\t  edge_,\n\t  \
internalEdgeLabels_Association,\n\t  antiParticleRules_Association\n\t] := \
Module[\n\t  {endpointParticle, oppositeVertex, oppositeParticle}, \n\t  \n\t \
 endpointParticle = internalEdgeLabels[edge][vertex];\n\t  oppositeVertex = \
SelectFirst[List @@ edge, # =!= vertex &];\n\t  oppositeParticle = \
internalEdgeLabels[edge][oppositeVertex];\n\t  \n\t  \
If[Lookup[antiParticleRules, endpointParticle, Missing[\"NotFound\"]] === \
oppositeParticle, \n\t    \"Upper\", \n\t    If[Lookup[antiParticleRules, \
oppositeParticle, Missing[\"NotFound\"]] === endpointParticle, \n\t      \
\"Lower\", \n\t      \"Upper\"\n\t    ]\n\t  ]\n\t]\n\t\n\
symmetrizeIndices[expr_, inds_List] := Module[\n\t  {perms}, \n\t  perms = \
Permutations[inds];\n\t  Total[(expr /. Thread[inds -> #]) & /@ perms] / \
Length[perms]\n\t]\n\t\nmakeVertexSpinIndicesExplicit[\n\t  \
vertexStructure_Association,\n\t  vertex_,\n\t  diag_,\n\t  \
edgeIndexData_Association,\n\t  antiParticleRules_Association\n\t] := Module[\
\n\t  {\n\t    expr, incidentLegs, internalSpinorLegs, groupedByIndex, \
replacementRules, \n\t    symmetrizationGroups, newExpr\n\t  },\n\t  \n\t  \
expr = vertexStructure[\"Expression\"];\n\t  incidentLegs = \
diag[\"IncidentLegData\"][vertex];\n\t  \n\t  internalSpinorLegs = Cases[\n\t \
   expr,\n\t    s : Spinor[\"Spin\", sa_, mp_Multiparticle] :> <|\n\t      \
\"Spinor\" -> s,\n\t      \"SpinType\" -> sa,\n\t      \"IndexLabel\" -> mp\n\
\t    |>,\n\t    Infinity\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  If[internalSpinorLegs === {}, \
Return[vertexStructure]];\n\t  \n\t  groupedByIndex = GroupBy[\n\t    \
internalSpinorLegs,\n\t    Function[item,\n\t      SelectFirst[\n\t        \
incidentLegs,\n\t        #[\"Kind\"] === \"Internal\" && #[\"Index\"] === \
item[\"IndexLabel\"] &\n\t      ][\"Source\"]\n\t    ]\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  \
replacementRules = Flatten @ KeyValueMap[\n\t    Function[{edge, \
spinorsForEdge},\n\t      Module[\n\t        {inds, variance, vertexLocal, \
orderedSpinors},\n\t        \n\t        vertexLocal = vertex;\n\t        \
variance = spinorVarianceAtEndpoint[\n\t          vertexLocal,\n\t          \
edge,\n\t          diag[\"InternalEdgeLabels\"],\n\t          \
antiParticleRules\n\t        ];\n\t        \n\t        inds = \
edgeIndexData[edge];\n\t        orderedSpinors = spinorsForEdge;\n\t        \n\
\t        MapThread[\n\t          (#1[\"Spinor\"] :> \n\t            \
Spinor[\"Spin\", variance, #1[\"SpinType\"], #1[\"IndexLabel\"], #2]) &,\n\t  \
        {orderedSpinors, inds}\n\t        ]\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    \
groupedByIndex\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  newExpr = expr /. replacementRules;\n\t  \n\
\t  symmetrizationGroups = Select[\n\t    Normal[groupedByIndex],\n\t    \
Length[Last[#]] > 1 &\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  newExpr = Fold[\n\t    \
Function[{currentExpr, group},\n\t      Module[{edge, inds},\n\t        edge \
= First[group];\n\t        inds = edgeIndexData[edge];\n\t        \
symmetrizeIndices[currentExpr, inds]\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    newExpr,\n\t \
   symmetrizationGroups\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  Join[vertexStructure, \
<|\"Expression\" -> newExpr|>]\n\t]\n\t\n\
makeDiagramSpinIndicesExplicit[diag_, antiParticleRules_Association] := \
Module[\n\t  {internalEdges, multiplicities, edgeIndexData, \
newVertexStructures},\n\t  \n\t  internalEdges = \
Keys[diag[\"InternalEdgeLabels\"]];\n\t  \n\t  multiplicities = Association @ \
KeyValueMap[\n\t    Function[{vertex, structures},\n\t      Sequence @@ {}\n\t\
    ],\n\t    diag[\"VertexStructures\"]\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  multiplicities = \
AssociationMap[\n\t    Function[edge,\n\t      Max[\n\t        1,\n\t        \
Sequence @@ Flatten @ KeyValueMap[\n\t          Function[{vertex, \
structures},\n\t            Cases[\n\t              structures,\n\t           \
   vs_Association :> Count[\n\t                Cases[\n\t                  \
vs[\"Expression\"],\n\t                  Spinor[\"Spin\", _, mp_] /; mp === \
diag[\"InternalEdgeIndices\"][edge][vertex],\n\t                  Infinity\n\t\
                ],\n\t                _\n\t              ]\n\t            ]\n\
\t          ],\n\t          Select[\n\t            \
diag[\"VertexStructures\"],\n\t            \
KeyMemberQ[diag[\"InternalEdgeIndices\"][edge], #] &\n\t          ]\n\t       \
 ]\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    internalEdges\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  edgeIndexData \
= Association @ MapIndexed[\n\t    Function[{edge, k},\n\t      edge -> \
Array[\n\t        Symbol[\"i\" <> ToString[#]] &,\n\t        \
multiplicities[edge],\n\t        Total[Take[Values[multiplicities], First[k] \
- 1]] + 1\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    internalEdges\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  \
newVertexStructures = Association @ KeyValueMap[\n\t    Function[{vertex, \
structures},\n\t      vertex -> Map[\n\t        \
makeVertexSpinIndicesExplicit[\n\t          #,\n\t          vertex,\n\t       \
   diag,\n\t          edgeIndexData,\n\t          antiParticleRules\n\t       \
 ] &,\n\t        structures\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    \
diag[\"VertexStructures\"]\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  Join[\n\t    diag,\n\t    <|\n\t\
      \"VertexStructures\" -> newVertexStructures,\n\t      \"SpinIndices\" \
-> edgeIndexData\n\t    |>\n\t  ]\n\t]\n```\n\nThen update your amplitude \
function:\n\n```wl\ndiagramAmplitude[diag_, antiParticleRules_Association] := \
Module[\n\t  {processed, vertexFactors, propagatorFactors},\n\t  \n\t  \
processed = makeDiagramSpinIndicesExplicit[diag, antiParticleRules];\n\t  \n\t\
  vertexFactors = Replace[\n\t    Values[processed[\"VertexStructures\"]],\n\t\
    {\n\t      {} :> 1,\n\t      list_List :> Lookup[Last[list], \"Expression\
\", 1]\n\t    },\n\t    1\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  propagatorFactors = Lookup[\n\t  \
  Values[processed[\"Propagators\"]],\n\t    \"Factor\",\n\t    1\n\t  ];\n\t \
 \n\t  Times @@ Join[vertexFactors, propagatorFactors] / I\n\t]\n```\n\nand \
for your SM model:\n\n```wl\nsmAntiParticleRules = \
antiParticleRulesFromModel[sm];\n```\n\nthen\n\n```wl\n\
diagramAmplitude[diags[[1]], smAntiParticleRules]\n```\n\n## Why this fixes \
your problem\n\nFor an internal edge labeled like\n\n```wl\nUndirectedEdge[u, \
v] -> <|u -> \"e\", v -> \"E\"|>\n```\n\nthe code now gives:\n\n* at vertex \
``u``: ``Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Upper\", ... , i1]``\n* at vertex ``v``: \
``Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Lower\", ... , i1]``\n\nSo:\n* variance matches particle \
vs antiparticle end\n* the same propagator carries the same index on both \
ends\n\n## One caution\n\nThis line:\n\n```wl\nSpinor[\"Spin\", _, mp_] /; mp \
=== diag[\"InternalEdgeIndices\"][edge][vertex]\n```\n\nassumes the relevant \
internal spinor argument is exactly the ``Multiparticle[...]`` stored in \
``diag[\"InternalEdgeIndices\"]``. From your earlier code, that appears to be \
correct. If HEPCAT sometimes wraps that object differently, we may need to \
broaden the match.\n\n## If you want\n\nI can give you a cleaner, shorter \
version next that:\n* computes the edge-index multiplicities more robustly,\n\
* stores spin-index data directly in the propagator record,\n* and integrates \
this automatically into [CreateDiagrams](paclet:ref/CreateDiagrams)-style \
output so ``diagramAmplitude[diag]`` needs no second argument.", "ChatData" -> 
